f=json.loads((O/'fit.json').read_text());r=json.loads((O/'construction.json').read_text());sp=json.loads((O/'spec.json').read_text())
marks=''
for i,a in enumerate(f['anchors'],1):
 x,y=a['referenceViewportPixel'];u,v=a['projectedViewportPixel'];color='#19ffb4' if a['use']=='fit' else '#24dfff'
 marks+=f'<line x1="{x}" y1="{y}" x2="{u}" y2="{v}" stroke="#ffe568"/><circle cx="{x}" cy="{y}" r="5" fill="none" stroke="{color}"/><path d="M{u-4},{v-4}l8,8m0,-8l-8,8" stroke="#ff4a70"/><text x="{x+7}" y="{y}" font-size="16" fill="white" stroke="#222" stroke-width="2" paint-order="stroke">{i}</text>'
rows=''.join(f'<tr><td>{i}</td><td>{html.escape(a["name"])}</td><td>{a["use"]}</td><td>{a["residualPixels"]:.2f}</td></tr>' for i,a in enumerate(f['anchors'],1))
page='''<!doctype html><html lang="en"><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1"><title>Central hall · first bay construction</title><style>
*{box-sizing:border-box}body{margin:0;background:#eef1ed;color:#203b32;font:16px/1.55 system-ui}main{max-width:1320px;margin:auto;padding:32px}h1{font-size:clamp(32px,4vw,50px);line-height:1.12;max-width:980px}h2{font-size:24px;margin-top:32px}a{color:#17614d}nav{display:flex;gap:18px;flex-wrap:wrap}.tag,.small{font-size:13px;color:#516a5d}.notice{padding:18px;border-left:4px solid #ad7b1b;background:#fff0d1}.grid{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(2,minmax(0,1fr));gap:22px}figure{margin:0}img{display:block;width:100%;height:auto}figcaption{font-size:13px;margin-top:9px}.stage{background:#172822;padding:15px;color:white;border-radius:8px}.stage svg{width:100%;height:auto;display:block}label{display:block;margin:10px 0}select,input{font:inherit;max-width:100%}select{padding:8px}input[type=range]{width:min(450px,100%)}table{border-collapse:collapse;width:100%;font-size:14px}th,td{padding:8px;text-align:left;border-bottom:1px solid #c8d4cb;overflow-wrap:anywhere}.table-wrap{overflow:auto}li{margin:8px 0}@media(max-width:700px){main{padding:18px}.grid{grid-template-columns:1fr}}
</style><main><header><div class="tag">KYOTO STATION / REPRESENTATIVE HALL BAY / 27 SEPTEMBER 2026</div><h1>From a flattened facade to a bay with depth.</h1><p>A new construction study uses the city mesh’s gate opening and upper-bay coordinates, with a provisional return depth inferred from the July 2026 photograph. Stone panels, joints, recessed openings, glazing, frames, soffit and a small floor sample now have original geometry and materials.</p><nav><a href="../../index.html">Research library</a><a href="../CENTRAL-HALL-CONSTRUCTION.md">Evidence and remaining work</a><a href="../hall-lighting/index.html">Photographs and lighting sources</a></nav><p class="notice"><strong>Uninstalled component.</strong> This is a construction study under static inspection lighting. It does not show the actual game or pass the representative-area milestone. Wider hall registration, canopy bearings, neighboring bays, shop/forecourt interfaces and final light/material response remain open.</p></header>
<section><h2>July 2026 photograph and fitted pose</h2><div class="stage"><label>Layer <select id="layer"><option value="source.png">Unmodified city mesh</option><option value="component.png">Isolated bay component</option></select></label><label>Model opacity <input id="opacity" type="range" min="0" max="1" step=".01" value=".45"></label><label><input type="checkbox" id="markers" checked> Fit points and withheld checks</label><svg viewBox="0 0 1200 800" aria-label="Photo overlay with source geometry or isolated component"><image href="../../photos/hall-maeda-2026.jpg" width="1200" height="800" preserveAspectRatio="xMidYMid slice"/><image id="model" href="source.png" width="1200" height="800" opacity=".45"/><g id="points">'''+marks+'''</g></svg><p class="small" style="color:#d2e2d8">Green: observations used in fitting. Cyan: withheld observations. Red: projected source vertices. The photograph is uniformly scaled and vertically cropped by 0.075 px, without perspective warping. Blue areas in the component layer are its empty inspection background.</p></div><p>The eight selected anchors pass the unchanged 24 px limit at 1200 px width and are visible in the original city model. The wider concourse and floor openings are not validated by these nearly coplanar anchors; this supplementary pose does not complete the broad hall acceptance view.</p></section>
<section><h2>Construction and close detail</h2><div class="grid"><figure><img src="component.png" alt="Isolated gate and upper bay from the supplementary photo camera"><figcaption>Gate width 16.999 m from the source mesh, with one upper bay. Those are model coordinates, not survey measurements. The component is incomplete around its outer edges.</figcaption></figure><figure><img src="close.png" alt="Close view of rose and dark stone frames with side glazing"><figcaption>Real openings and side returns replace a flat texture. The sample still lacks believable indirect light, edge wear and the final glazing response. The periodic stone pattern found in the first render has been removed.</figcaption></figure></div></section>
<section><h2>Stone at walking eye height</h2><figure><img src="walking-detail.png" alt="Close stone panel sample viewed from 1.6 metres above the component floor"><figcaption>Original stone grain and recessed joints. The sharp edges and bright grazing-angle seams still need bevel and occlusion work. This is an inspection pose, not a native walking test.</figcaption></figure></section><section><h2>Measured scope and limits</h2><ul><li>7,800 triangles, 650 closed panels, 537 colliding panels, eight material batches.</li><li>Nine original 512 px material maps; 2.73 MB raw component GLB and 12 MiB calculated RGBA+mip storage. These are resource counts, not a gameplay benchmark.</li><li>Side depth rounds to 5.6 m from three independent image picks, conditioned on the source side plane and fitted camera. Hidden closures and module spacing remain inferred.</li><li>All emitted vertices, triangle indices, winding and face normals pass independent checks. All 6,444 native triangle probes pass; maximum hit difference is 0.00285 mm. This does not prove full-station routes or gameplay.</li></ul></section>
<section><h2>Camera residuals</h2><p>Six fitted and two withheld landmarks. Fit RMS 7.09 px; maximum withheld error 22.09 px against 24 px. Focal length 2104.75 original-image pixels; no optimizer bound is active. Camera sensitivity excludes lens, crop and source-geometry errors.</p><div class="table-wrap"><table><thead><tr><th>#</th><th>Feature</th><th>Role</th><th>Error(px)</th></tr></thead><tbody>'''+rows+'''</tbody></table></div></section><section><h2>Evidence receipts</h2><nav>'''+''.join(f'<a href="{fn}">{label}</a>' for fn,label in [('fit.json','Fit and sensitivity'),('visibility.json','Visibility audit'),('source-proof.json','Exact vertex proof'),('spec.json','Source/depth specification'),('construction.json','Construction report'),('serialization.json','Browser/native serialization'),('normals.json','Face normals'),('native.json','All 6,444 native probes'),('fit-tool-regression.json','Fitting-tool regression'),('render-photo.json','Render receipt')])+'''</nav><p class="small">The initial portrait fits remain rejected in the earlier study. Full station remains courtyard life04/browser04. No service, scoring or production change.</p></section></main><script>const model=document.querySelector('#model');document.querySelector('#layer').onchange=e=>model.setAttribute('href',e.target.value);document.querySelector('#opacity').oninput=e=>model.setAttribute('opacity',e.target.value);document.querySelector('#markers').onchange=e=>document.querySelector('#points').style.display=e.target.checked?'':'none';</script></html>'''
(O/'index.html').write_text(page)
(O/'publication-receipt.json').write_text(json.dumps({'files':{name:hashlib.sha256((O/name).read_bytes()).hexdigest() for name in files},'fullStationChanged':False,'finalVisualAcceptance':False},indent=2)+'\n')
print(O/'index.html')
